From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Mitchell <me@gmitch215.xyz>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:05:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: pass System V IPC commands without IPC_64

The wasm kernel uses the asm-generic syscall table, whose shmctl,
semctl and msgctl take the command as is and always use the 64-bit
structures. musl ORs IPC_64 (0x100) into every command unless the arch
defines it as 0, which aarch64, riscv32, or1k and the other generic
arches do. Without it IPC_STAT, IPC_SET and IPC_RMID all reached the
kernel as unknown commands and failed with EINVAL, so a segment could
be neither inspected nor removed.
---
diff --git a/arch/wasm/syscall_arch.h b/arch/wasm/syscall_arch.h
--- a/arch/wasm/syscall_arch.h
+++ b/arch/wasm/syscall_arch.h
@@ -10,3 +10,5 @@ extern long __syscall3(long n, long a, long b, long c);
 extern long __syscall4(long n, long a, long b, long c, long d);
 extern long __syscall5(long n, long a, long b, long c, long d, long e);
 extern long __syscall6(long n, long a, long b, long c, long d, long e, long f);
+
+#define IPC_64 0
